		(locked yes)
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "91be440a-c2fe-4724-b5d1-38429f8fca98")
		(at 150.35 132.5)
		(descr "LED, 3.0 mm, 2 pins. Land pattern is RECENTRED against KiCad's stock LED_THT:LED_D3.0mm: pads sit at -1.27 and +1.27 with the body centred on the footprint origin, where the stock footprint puts pad 1 at the origin and the body at +1.27. That is why the 3D model carries an offset of -1.27 in x: LED_D3.0mm.step is drawn for the stock footprint and its solid spans x -0.230 to 2.770, centred on 1.270. Without the offset the LED renders one half-pitch off its own hole. Do not zero the offset - the board is correct and only the render moves. Pads named C (square, cathode) and A, for symbols that number LED pins A/C (shieldXL's Eagle LEDs).")
